Chapter: IdmReadLine
  cites Kernel chapter IdentityManager

 `idm-read-line-bytes` loops until Enter. It read `uefi-read-key` -- the
 raw PS/2 Set-1 make code -- and compared the result against ASCII 13.
 Enter's make code is 28, so the comparison could never hold: the loop ran
 forever, and every byte it collected was a scancode rather than a
 character. The passphrase prompt could not be answered, which is what the
 skip reason "blocks waiting for keyboard input" had been reporting all
 along, in the voice of an environment limitation.

Section: Definitions

  irl-show : List Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Console] Integer
  irl-show (xs) (i) (len) =
    if i >= len then 0
    else act
      print-line-uni (integer-to-text (list-at xs i))
      irl-show xs (i + 1) len
    end

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let bs = idm-read-line-bytes
    in act
      print-line-uni (integer-to-text (list-length bs))
      irl-show bs 0 (list-length bs)
      print-line-uni "returned"
    end
  end
